**The records establish an affirmative CIA hold on information intended for the FBI. They do not independently authenticate the further claim that CIA directed a Saudi-mediated recruitment operation or imposed the hold to protect it.** I found no authenticated connection to Urban Moving Systems or its personnel in the material reviewed.

The nine-page report includes the chronology, witness-by-witness assessment, competing explanations, evidence that would challenge each hypothesis, and exact source/page citations:

[:chatgpt-content-reference{index="5"}](https://chatgpt.com/library?file_id=libfile_eb3f88c376c08191acb72476404ea08f&account_id=personal)

### Principal findings

- **The hold is documented; its motive remains unresolved.** On January 5, 2000, CIA officer “Michelle” entered the hold, attributing it to deputy chief “John.” CIA OIG identifies the unanswered follow-up as **January 13**, resolving a five-versus-eight-day inconsistency within DOJ’s account. An internal CIA cable asserted that visa documents had already reached the FBI, but investigators could not corroborate that transfer. See DOJ pp. 240–243, 250; CIA pp. 53–55. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="0"}

- **Saudi intelligence affiliation and CIA tasking are separate evidentiary questions.** The June 2017 memorandum reports GIP payments through Bandar, but its source and reporting date are redacted. It supplies no CIA recruitment order. Canestraro’s CS-23 allegations on printed pp. 20–21 describe operational files and consular instructions without supplying those files, identified witnesses or their original accounts. AE827 presents a defense discovery argument; it does not establish those allegations judicially. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="1"}

- **The FBI closure and civil ruling answer different questions.** The 2021 FBI assessment found insufficient evidence for the contemplated criminal prosecution. The August 2025 court made substantive, preliminary jurisdictional inferences after discovery, applying the stated preponderance burdens. Its Saudi-employment and assistance findings were more than acceptance of pleadings, but neither a final liability verdict nor authentication of CIA direction. See closure pp. 9–11; ruling pp. 6–9, 35, 39–45. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="2"}

- **The interview correction is narrow:** approximately **60 interviews during 2007–2016**, concerning Encore’s main subjects and known associates, voluntarily and through the grand jury. It does not mean 60 distinct people or all September 11 investigative interviews. See addendum p. 3, EO14040-000014. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="3"}

The smallest useful missing-record set comprises the original hold/transmission trail; the 2017 source and alleged liaison/tasking records; original witness statements and closure-supporting records; and existing UMS cross-references.

**Existing request coverage remains unverified:** I could not retrieve the current tracker or relevant original receipts. The report therefore identifies record targets without assuming a pending request covers them. No requests were sent.
